      "run": 0,
      "steps": 4,
      "narrative": "I'm not entirely sure how I ended up in this cramped galley, but as I look around, I can see that it's been some time since I was last on dry land. The air is thick with the smell of salt, and it's clear that the sea has taken its toll on everything. I've been trying to make sense of my surroundings, and I've spent some time examining a kettle that was lying on the floor. It's a simple tin kettle, dented on one side, but it's the only clue I have about what might have happened here.\n\nI've been trying to think about what to do next, and I've been eyeing the doorway to the north, wondering what kind of answers I might find there. I've also considered going down the hatch to the south, but something about it feels ominous. For now, though, I'm just trying to piece together what's happened to me and how I can get back to where I belong.",
